cctext patch 0006: filter effects.

lunasvg 3.5.0 ignores <filter> and the filter property: a draw.io "Shadow",
a Mermaid 12 node shadow (feDropShadow) or a CSS drop-shadow() drew flat,
and a blurred or recoloured element drew unfiltered. resvg's test suite:
82 of 398 filter tests "passed" (their expected output happens to be
unfiltered); 257 now.

New files source/svgfilterelement.{h,cpp}:
- <filter> (x / y / width / height, filterUnits, primitiveUnits,
  xlink:href inheritance of attributes and primitives, cycles ignored) and
  the primitives feGaussianBlur (three box blurs as the spec describes, a
  true Gaussian kernel below d = 2), feOffset, feFlood, feMerge,
  feComposite (over / in / out / atop / xor / arithmetic / lighter),
  feColorMatrix, feBlend (all separable and non-separable modes),
  feComponentTransfer and feDropShadow; the other primitives (feImage,
  feTile, feTurbulence, feMorphology, lighting, feConvolveMatrix,
  feDisplacementMap) pass their input through.
- in / in2 / result (SourceGraphic, SourceAlpha; BackgroundImage,
  FillPaint and StrokePaint read as the source, as resvg does), primitive
  subregions, color-interpolation-filters (linearRGB by default, sRGB),
  flood-color / flood-opacity (with explicit inherit).
- CSS filter functions: blur(), drop-shadow(), grayscale(), sepia(),
  saturate(), hue-rotate(), invert(), opacity(), brightness(), contrast()
  and url() in a list.
- A filter runs on the element's offscreen canvas in device pixels
  (deviations and offsets scaled by the current transform); the canvas
  covers the whole filter region when it fits the pixel limit, so content
  outside the view still blurs or shifts in.
- Its canvas is the filter region cut to what the filter can bring into
  view: the parent canvas grown by the filter's reach (3 deviations per
  blur plus every offset). Blurs touch only the painted pixels grown by
  their reach, and run their vertical pass on a transposed copy.
- Bounded by lunasvg_set_filter_limits() (include/lunasvg.h): the filter
  region in device pixels (larger: drawn unfiltered), the blur deviation
  (clamped), primitives per filter (the rest ignored), the bytes of live
  intermediate images, and one render's filter work (primitives x region
  pixels, blurs weighted; Document::render resets it): past the last two
  the element draws unfiltered. Every buffer is a checked malloc;
  coordinates are clamped before float -> int.

Changes elsewhere: the element ids, attribute and CSS property names
(svgelement / svgproperty), the filter / flood / color-interpolation-
filters properties (svglayoutstate), SVGBlendInfo and begin/endGroup
(svgrenderstate: the filter runs before clip-path, mask and opacity), a
filtered element's paint box is its filter region and a container's
includes its filtered descendants', an invalid filter reference draws
nothing (Filter Effects 1), and paintBoundingBox's assertion on a
non-finite box became "empty" (it fired on fuzzed coordinates once
descendants' boxes were asked).

Known gaps: a rotated or skewed element's filter runs along the device
axes (resvg's complex-transform tests); feImage, feTile, feTurbulence,
feMorphology, the lighting filters, feConvolveMatrix and
feDisplacementMap are not implemented.

Apply after 0005.

